# AIDR - English UI & Errors

User-facing text in **aidr-fe** and **aidr-be** must be **English**.

## Must be English

1. **UI copy** - labels, buttons, placeholders, titles, breadcrumbs, empty states, toasts, confirm dialogs, aria-labels, tooltips.
2. **Validation messages** - FE helpers (`validators`, form validation) and BE `AppException` / `NotFoundException` / `ConflictException` messages returned to the client.
3. **API error payloads** - ProblemDetails `detail` / `title` / `message` shown to users.
4. **Transactional email** sent to users (reset password, etc.).

## Allowed Vietnamese

- Internal docs (`docs/`), Cursor rules, and commit/PR notes.
- Vietnamese **data** (category names, product names, addresses) entered by users.
- Comments may be English or Vietnamese; prefer English for new code comments.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌
<button>Lưu thay đổi</button>
throw new Error('Không tạo được danh mục.');

// ✅
<button>Save changes</button>
throw new Error('Unable to create category.');
```

```csharp
// ❌
throw new AppException("Tên danh mục là bắt buộc.");

// ✅
throw new AppException("Category name is required.");
```

## Do not

- Mix Vietnamese and English on the same screen for chrome/errors.
- Put use-case codes (`UC-22`) in UI copy.
